    "created_at": "2016-03-08T16:14:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-08T16:34:40Z",
    "body": "> As an example, how should \"The VideoTrackList.selectedIndex attribute must return the index of the currently selected track, if any.\" be rephrased?\n\nVideoTrackList's selectedIndex attribute must return the index of the currently selected track, if any.\n\n> Doesn't \"ProgressEvent's lengthComputable attribute\" also make it sound like the ProgressEvent interface object has a lengthComputable attribute?\n\nI don't think so. Interfaces have attributes, which are denoted in code through `InterfaceName.prototype.attributeName` (not `InterfaceName.attributeName`).\n",
